{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1558655-new-shadow-gift-gift-of-resonation","id":1558655,"title":"[New Shadow Gift] Gift of Resonation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-05T00:43:17-08:00","id":1558655,"title":"[New Shadow Gift] Gift of Resonation","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Shadow Gift is my first real attempt at an entire gift that isn't a Moon Gift draft or a Wolf Gift. I made it trying to follow Chris Allen's advice on his patreon and other guides, but unlike my Gift of the Chase (Wolf Gift) I'm not as satisfied with this draft. I don't think it's outright bad or has poor ideas, but despite how much I like it, I don't necessarily know if the basis for the Gift really works all that well. I think sound could certainly be a power that gets interpreted as a Shadow Gift by the lense of Father Wolf, but I need to think about it a little more and some opinions might help. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The concept of resonance overall is something I wanted to tackle on a spiritual level as well as the typical meaning and I thought it would be fun</span></span> to try and mix some spiritual shenanigans with confusing/damage the hearing of prey.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gift of Resonation</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Gift of Resonation is an often misleading gift as it appeals to both the resonance of sound, and the spiritual resonance of the Hisil. It draws on connection, the connection of one\u2019s movements to the ripples they make physically and spiritually, amplifying an Uratha\u2019s or prey\u2019s ears to the metaphysical impressions of those around them rather than strictly physical noise, though Uratha and prey both often confuse this gift\u2019s effects with the latter.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shadow\u2019s Whisper (Cunning)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After resonating with her prey\u2019s noise, and through a phenomenon similar to reaching, the Uratha may separate sound from herself by throwing it temporarily across the gauntlet, confusing the prey's senses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Survival + Cunning versus Composure + Primal Urge</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 scene</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Facet can be used against a single prey that the Uratha can perceive, though she must be able to hear the prey.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Uratha\u2019s sense of hearing runs wild for the remainder of the scene. Her bonus to perception from wolf senses disappears and she suffers a penalty to perception equal to her own Cunning renown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Facet fails. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The prey\u2019s sense of hearing involving the Uratha distorts. Any noise that comes from the Uratha as a result of their movement, speech, actions not involving outside tools are instead heard from a direction of the Uratha\u2019s choice. Sounds heard as a result of a tool with minimum interaction from the Uratha come from the proper direction (A gun being fired, a jackhammer, a phone alarm).</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> This facet is able to target any number of prey the Uratha can perceive and hear.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Deafening Rhythm (Glory)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha lets loose a powerful and dangerous howl, as terrifying as it is loud, causing the prey\u2019s heartbeat to rise to their ears. Even heartless creatures find their auditory senses overwhelmed with the sound of their own fear.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Stamina + Intimidation + Glory - Stamina</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 turn per success rolled</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This facet affects everyone except the Uratha within the Uratha\u2019s Glory in yards. If affecting multiple prey, the Uratha subtracts the highest Stamina of all her prey from the roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Uratha gains the Ban Condition. Her own voice fills her with a soul shattering dread and she cannot speak. Hearing any recording of her voice or mimicry of it will cause her to flee the source of the noise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Facet fails.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every success on the activation roll deals a point of bashing damage to the affected prey and causes them to suffer the Deafened Tilt for a turn per success rolled as their heartbeat blots out all noise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Deafened Tilt instead lasts until the scene ends.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Camouflage Resonance (Honor)</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha enhances her connection to the ambient essence in the air around her, attuning to the various resonances in her area, both in the flesh and shadow. Spirits who stumble upon the Uratha now find her a viable source of essence, and are keen to be allowed near her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 5 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Composure + Empathy + Honor</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended (15 successes; each roll represents 1 hour)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 day</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As use of this facet requires attuning to both the Gurihal and Hisil, the dice pool of Perfect Resonance is penalized according to the Gauntlet Strength chart on page 101.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Roll Results</i></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Uratha\u2019s essence appears tainted from the outside looking in. He registers as a magath to other spirits and counts as having the Resonant Condition for other magath. Their essence remains tainted until they absorb their Honor renown in essence of a singular resonance without any other in between.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No successes are acquired, and the Uratha gains the Stumbled Condition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha counts as having the Resonant Condition towards spirits of every influence and improves her first impression to non-hostile spirits by two steps. Spirits will naturally flock to the Uratha seeing her as a source of nourishment, able to regain a point of essence from her as the Resonant Condition counts as being tagged to them without risk of becoming magath. While unable to properly gorge themselves on essence from her, the Uratha must be careful, as any essence fed to spirits comes from her own reserves. Each day, each point of essence gained by spirits as a result of this condition beyond her Honor Renown, the Uratha loses a point of essence. This facet ends early if the Uratha runs out of essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha may have spirits gain twice her Honor Renown in essence before it begins to be taken from her own reserves.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Perfect Pitch (Purity)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha\u2019s control over resonation isn\u2019t as powerful as a spirit\u2019s influence, but she can still forcibly connect herself to a sound\u2019s point of origin, bestowing her even more supernaturally powerful recognition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 scene</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Uratha gains a bonus to hearing based Perception rolls equal to her Purity Renown for the duration of the facet. The Uratha also gains a supernatural form of perfect pitch. She is able to identify and replicate music notes, as well as other sounds she hears. As long as the Uratha manages to gather at least a single success on a Perception roll to hear a sound, she is able to identify the broad origin of the sound. Footsteps become immediately identifiable as coming from the animal that made them, the rumblings of an engine in the forest are identifiable as belonging specifically to a car or motorbike. This facet does not reveal exact details beyond the noise\u2019s broad origin, such as being unable to tell you exactly what kind of dog is making those footsteps, or the exact model of motorbike\u2019s engine that is rumbling. The Uratha is able to perfectly replicate any sound she has heard during usage of this facet for the duration of the facet, even if she would normally be incapable of doing so.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Claw On The Pulse (Wisdom)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By concentrating, an Uratha can accurately detect the pulse and resonance of prey within her immediate area, bypassing even supernatural silence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Essence</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Scene</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background noise quiets as the Uratha stands still, sharpening her spiritual senses within 100 x the werewolf\u2019s Wisdom Renown yards in radius around her, allowing her to sense the resonance of spirits or locations within this area. This resonance can only be sensed while you and the resonance\u2019s source are on the same side of the gauntlet. The Uratha can detect physical creatures on the same side of the gauntlet, bypassing supernatural methods of obfuscation, within this radius, sensing their distance and direction in correlation to her. This facet ends if the Uratha moves in any major way, such as walking, attacking, or dodging.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28400-sigvardthediablerist","name":"SigvardTheDiablerist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28400_1.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}